<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fructuoso Rivera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1784">1784</a>–<a href="/years/1854">1854</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fructuoso Rivera was a Uruguayan caudillo and soldier who became the first constitutional president of the Oriental Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> in 1830. A veteran of Artigas's struggles and the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a> party, and his rivalry with Manuel Oribe and the Blancos led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguayan-civil-war">Guerra Grande</a> of 1839 to 1851. He served as president again from 1839 to 1843.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fructuoso-rivera.jpg" alt="Fructuoso Rivera" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan Manuel Blanes · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_Manuel_Blanes_-_Retrato_del_General_Fructuoso_Rivera.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
